  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 223 PM CDT Mon Oct 12 2026\n\nLow chances for rain will continue through mid-week each afternoon \ndue to seabreeze interactions. We are pleasantly expecting our first \narctic cold front late this week. NBM currently has highs in the 80s \nthis weekend with lows in the 50s and 60s, however, some models are \nshowing cooler temperatures for this weekend. This will be something \nthat we will need to fine tune as the event gets closer. Another \naspect of the forecast that will need to be fine tuned is the wind \npotential. As of this moment, strong winds are expected that will \nlead to Small Craft Advisory conditions but remaining below Gale. \nSome probabilistic models though are showing a low chance for Gale \nforce winds in the wake of the front. Although rain chances have \ndecreased a bit from previous forecast, showers and thunderstorms \nwill still be possible with the frontal passage. \n\nWarm temperatures will continue with highs in the 90s through mid-\nweek before the cold front. Heat index values for the next couple of \ndays will range from 106-111 degrees along with a moderate to major \nrisk of heat-related impacts. Please remember to continue to \npractice heat safety: take breaks when outside, drink plenty of \nwater, and look before you lock.",
